  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## The Keeper
    
    Totatirus~ Domina was a Nightshelf guild-master who abandoned her position at The Fissured Smelt~ — a geothermal vent-works in the Berg's eastern tunnels — to take up solitary guardianship of Scar☽ Sanctcaetiata, a geological anomaly near the thermal vents of The Drowned Ledge. The anomaly pulses with properties inconsistent with the Berg's known geology. Totatirus~ made it her life's work to ensure no one understood what it was, a mission she pursued through isolation, cipher, and deliberate obfuscation.
    
    Her shelter was carved into the ledge's western face, heated by fire-core braziers she maintained without interruption — by her own account, from fear of darkness rather than ritual obligation. Her flippers bore ore-handling scars. Her left ear was missing upper cartilage from an injury she refused to explain. She kept three journals in separate ciphers and burned them page by page into the steam vents, a practice that suggests either extraordinary paranoia or an understanding of ice-memory that most scholars lack.
    
    Thirty meters beneath her shelter lay the shadow-forge vault containing ☽'somunis' Mist~Record, a fire-core tome of pre-penguin history whose previous keepers — Augur ☽'Silvsiaelrous~ the Resolute, Noctisum~, and at least one unnamed reader during a Long Dark — either vanished, died, or withdrew into isolation. Totatirus~ was the last in this lineage. She did not read the tome, did not unwrap it, and opened the vault on no schedule. Whether this restraint was wisdom or the lesson of her predecessors' fates is left to the reader.
    
    She turned away three Nightshelf delegations, including one led by her sister Kael, who continued leaving supplies at the ledge's edge in silence. Her only communication was with orca scouts who breached the nearby ice, whom she warned away.
    
    ## Death at the Smelt
    
    Despite her seclusion, Totatirus~ still held guild-master rank, and her token — a fire-core carved into a closed flipper — hung above the main forge of The Fissured Smelt~, where she sat on the Shadow Parliament.
    
    When the Wake-Singers breached the Smelt through its mineral-water channels, Totatirus~ emerged from years of reclusion to fight. She drove back Scar-Matriarch Keth'nal at the eastern wall before being killed by Vel'keth the Younger. Her last words were cut short mid-sentence — the chronicles do not record them, and the ice-memory at that depth is too disrupted by the breach to recover.
    
    Her token still hangs above the abandoned forge. The Nightshelf built a shrine of two unfilled cups on a ledge where the steam rises.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
